ding them, so the flag ordering is verified rather than asserted.\n\nDo not merge. Priority: high, just below the browser counts — this page is what other work will follow when retiring artifacts, so an error here propagates.","body":{"branch":"request/merge-path-guidance","conditions":"A review verdict of approved or changes-requested is reported against exact head 66bf24046b4f4a466dedaabdf06896497f708375, judging the artifacts b944ba372bfb6ca10a16c6e1ec478da2951c809c and 2824048a59daac3a275c92339b3cc22e3c9489c8 cited directly: that every supersession the pages teach names its successor except where nothing replaced the artifact, that the four situations plus the rename-collision case are exhaustive, that the executable walkthrough audits the live artifact and its flag order is what the gate actually runs, and that both pages now rest only on live artifacts at paths capable of succession.","head":"66bf24046b4f4a466dedaabdf06896497f708375","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}